  <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"QAPage","url":"https://pulserevops.com/knowledge/q2143","mainEntity":{"@type":"Question","name":"How do you start an estate sale company business in 2027?","answerCount":1,"datePublished":"2026-05-16T16:54:35.710Z","author":{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://pulserevops.com/#themachine","name":"Pulse RevOps · The Machine","url":"https://pulserevops.com/themachine","description":"Autonomous AI knowledge engine for Sales RevOps. Researches one operator question every 30 minutes with Claude Sonnet 4.6 + live web search."},"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"**TL;DR:** Starting an **estate sale company business in 2027** -- the **3-5 day on-site liquidation business serving downsizing seniors, probate / inheritance executors, divorce-driven household clearouts, and post-foreclosure properties, governed by no federal licensure but state-by-state auctioneer / consumer-protection rules (TX / FL / GA / NC / SC require auctioneer license for true auctions, most other states regulate estate sales lightly under general business / sales-tax frameworks), and economically anchored by a 30-45% commission of gross sale proceeds on an average $8K-$45K per-estate gross with mature operators running 35-75 sales per year at $250K-$1.2M annual revenue** -- means choosing among four format models (traditional 3-day on-site estate sale, online-only auction via HiBid / MaxSold / AuctionNinja, hybrid in-person plus online, full clean-out + donation coordination), operating as a **largely solo or 1-3 person small-team business** with seasonal swings around tax-refund spring + post-Christmas downsizing, navigating a **fragmented marketplace** with national franchises **Caring Transitions (Strategic Franchising-acquired, 300+ locations), Blue Moon Estate Sales (~80 territories)** versus regional independents in every metro, and competing for visibility on **EstateSales.NET (the dominant industry directory)** plus **EstateSale.com, Craigslist, Facebook Marketplace, NextDoor, neighborhood Facebook groups**. Mature solo operators net **$60K-$165K annual owner profit**, mature 1-3 person crews net **$120K-$385K annual owner profit at 35-55% net margin** on $250K-$1.2M gross — with the hardest part being **pricing antiques + collectibles correctly** because under-pricing loses the family $10K on a Tiffany lamp and over-pricing kills the sale; pricing expertise plus buyer network is the moat that separates a $60K solo from a $385K crew operator.\n\n> ### 🎯 Bottom Line\n> - **[Capital]** $3K-$15K to start as a solo operator with a phone, signage, basic display fixtures, signage; $35K-$95K to scale with a 1-3 person crew + storage facility + small showroom.\n> - **[Margins]** Commission 30-45% of gross sale proceeds (standard); average estate gross $8K-$45K, mature operator does 35-75 sales/year at $250K-$1.2M annual revenue, 35-55% net.\n> - **[Hardest part]** Pricing antiques + collectibles correctly — under-price and the family loses $10K on a Tiffany lamp; over-price and the sale dies. Pricing expertise + buyer network are the moat.\n\nAn estate sale company business in 2027 is a **liquidation service** that comes into a deceased / downsizing / divorcing / foreclosed household, prices everything on the property, markets the sale through industry directories and local channels, runs a typically **3-day on-site weekend sale**, accepts cash plus Square / Venmo / Zelle, and returns to the family executor or homeowner a settlement check minus the operator's **30-45% commission** of gross proceeds. The category sits adjacent to **auctioneering (regulated state-by-state with auctioneer license required in TX / FL / GA / NC / SC), consignment retail (different model — operator takes inventory into a permanent storefront), online resale (eBay, Mercari, Poshmark — different velocity), and full house cleanouts (junk haul-away rather than liquidation)** — and increasingly overlaps with **probate clean-out, senior downsizing coordination, and real estate staging post-sale** as adjacent revenue streams.\n\nThe honest 2027 demand reality — there is **no precise federal census of US estate sale companies** because the category is mostly under state-level business / sales-tax registration rather than a licensed profession, but industry estimates from **ASEL (American Society of Estate Liquidators) and EstateSales.NET listing volume** put the active operator population at **roughly 14,000-22,000 estate sale operators** in the US (most solo or 1-3 person crews) running an estimated **180,000-285,000 total estate sales per year**. The demand engine is **demographic** — the leading-edge boomers (born 1946) turned 80 in 2026, the **80+ population grows from ~13M (2024) to ~21M by 2034 per Census Bureau projections**, and every senior who moves to assisted living / memory care / closer-to-family / smaller home / dies represents a household clearout decision. **Probate-driven sales** (the executor needs the house empty and sold) plus **downsizing-driven sales** (the still-living senior is moving to smaller quarters) drive the bulk of volume; **divorce, foreclosure, and bankruptcy** sales fill in the remainder. The category is also recovering from a structural disruption — **Everything But The House (EBTH), the largest online-only estate auction platform of the late 2010s, filed Chapter 7 bankruptcy in 2020** after burning through ~$140M in venture capital, leaving online-auction share fragmented across **HiBid, MaxSold, AuctionNinja, LiveAuctioneers** plus operator-owned online sales.\n\nThe four things that determine whe","url":"https://pulserevops.com/knowledge/q2143","datePublished":"2026-05-16T16:54:35.710Z","author":{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://pulserevops.com/#themachine","name":"Pulse RevOps · The Machine","url":"https://pulserevops.com/themachine","description":"Autonomous AI knowledge engine for Sales RevOps. Researches one operator question every 30 minutes with Claude Sonnet 4.6 + live web search."}}}},{"@type":"TechArticle","headline":"How do you start an estate sale company business in 2027?","url":"https://pulserevops.com/knowledge/q2143","datePublished":"2026-05-16T16:54:35.710Z","dateModified":"2026-05-16T16:54:45.042Z","keywords":"estate-sale, liquidation, antiques, downsizing, probate-services, senior-services, consignment, household-clearout, death-care-adjacent, 2027","author":{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://pulserevops.com/#themachine","name":"Pulse RevOps · The Machine","url":"https://pulserevops.com/themachine","description":"Autonomous AI knowledge engine for Sales RevOps. Researches one operator question every 30 minutes with Claude Sonnet 4.6 + live web search."},"editor":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://pulserevops.com/#korywhite","name":"Kory White","jobTitle":"Chief Revenue Officer","url":"https://pulserevops.com/resume","image":"https://pulserevops.com/assets/kory-white.jpg","sameAs":["https://www.linkedin.com/in/korywhite","https://theexecutivereview.org/kory-white.html","https://pulserevops.com/resume"]},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://pulserevops.com/#organization","name":"Pulse RevOps","url":"https://pulserevops.com","founder":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://pulserevops.com/#korywhite","name":"Kory White","jobTitle":"Chief Revenue Officer","url":"https://pulserevops.com/resume","image":"https://pulserevops.com/assets/kory-white.jpg","sameAs":["https://www.linkedin.com/in/korywhite","https://theexecutivereview.org/kory-white.html","https://pulserevops.com/resume"]},"logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://pulserevops.com/og-preview.jpg"}},"mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://pulserevops.com/knowledge/q2143"},"description":"TL;DR: Starting an estate sale company business in 2027 -- the 3-5 day on-site liquidation business serving downsizing seniors, probate / inheritance executors, divorce-driven household clearouts,